; soak-expunge: 20 rounds of vscsitest on the raw units (0-2) and an
; expunge, with free memory before and after. No filesystem may be mounted
; on vscsirs.device (the expunge must find nothing open).
; Logs: SHARED:vscsi/soak/expunge.log
FailAt 30
Copy SHARED:vscsi/vscsirs.device DEVS: QUIET
Copy SHARED:vscsi/vscsitest RAM: QUIET
Copy SHARED:vscsi/expunge RAM: QUIET
Protect RAM:vscsitest +rwed QUIET
Protect RAM:expunge +rwed QUIET
MakeDir SHARED:vscsi/soak >NIL:
Echo "start" >SHARED:vscsi/soak/expunge.log
Avail TOTAL >>SHARED:vscsi/soak/expunge.log
Set n 0
Lab round
RAM:vscsitest vscsirs.device 3 5 >RAM:vt.out
Search RAM:vt.out "tests passed" >>SHARED:vscsi/soak/expunge.log
RAM:expunge DEVICE vscsirs.device >NIL:
Set n `Eval $n + 1`
If VAL $n LT 20
  Skip round BACK
EndIf
Echo "end" >>SHARED:vscsi/soak/expunge.log
Avail FLUSH >NIL:
Avail TOTAL >>SHARED:vscsi/soak/expunge.log
Echo "soak-expunge done"
